1zpz|n|Having sense of feeling; possessing or exhibiting the capacity of receiving impressions from external objects; as, a sensitive soul. ; Having quick and acute sensibility, either to the action of external objects, or to impressions upon the mind and feelings; highly susceptible; easily and acutely affected. ; Having a capacity of being easily affected or moved; as, a sensitive thermometer; sensitive scales. ; Readily affected or changed by certain appropriate agents; as, silver chloride or bromide, when in contact with certain organic substances, is extremely sensitive to actinic rays. ; Serving to affect the sense; sensible. ; Of or pertaining to sensation; depending on sensation; as, sensitive motions; sensitive muscular motions excited by irritation.	N:1aik,30,4~1aik,30,4
