202z|n|One who, or that which, sets; -- used mostly in composition with a noun, as typesetter; or in combination with an adverb, as a setter on (or inciter), a setter up, a setter forth. ; A hunting dog of a special breed originally derived from a cross between the spaniel and the pointer. Modern setters are usually trained to indicate the position of game birds by standing in a fixed position, but originally they indicated it by sitting or crouching. ; One who hunts victims for sharpers. ; One who adapts words to music in composition. ; An adornment; a decoration; -- with off. ; A shallow seggar for porcelain.	a:s8l,73,3~s8l,73,3	n:zr,108,8;s8l,83,6~zr,108,8;s8l,83,6
